        "value": "<p>Method: High-Performance Liquid Chromatography (HPLC) / LC-MS/MS (specify if known)</p>\n<p>Test Result:</p>\n<p>| Parameter &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | Result &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | Reference Range* &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>|-----------------------|----------------|--------------------------------|<br>| Noradrenaline (Norepinephrine) | ______ &micro;g/24 hrs | 15 &ndash; 80 &micro;g/24 hrs (adults)** &nbsp; &nbsp;|</p>\n<p>*Reference ranges may vary slightly by laboratory. &nbsp;<br>**Pediatric or age-specific ranges may apply.</p>\n<p>Interpretation: &nbsp;<br>- **Elevated levels** may indicate pheochromocytoma, neuroblastoma, or other catecholamine-secreting tumors. &nbsp;<br>- **Low or normal levels** typically suggest absence of catecholamine excess. &nbsp;<br>- Clinical correlation and further endocrine or imaging evaluation may be necessary.</p>",
